            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of student perception of the lecture &quot;oral functional medical rehabilitation: balneophysiotherapy&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>875-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">Th aim of the study was to assess this course as perceived by the 6th year dentistry students.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Applying and validating the &quot;Dundee Ready Education Environment Measure (DREEM)&quot; for the first time in Romania.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS AND DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The reliability of the test according to Cronbach alpha method, which measures the internal consistency of a test, was 0.87 (Cronbach alpha coefficient should be above 0.70). As to the reliability coefficients (internal consistency) for each test subscale and for the entire test, DREEM proved a very good overall reliability, with alpha = 0.89. The reliability of each DREEM subscale was also analyzed. The DREEM test results, with a global score of 149, indicate a &quot;more positive than negative&quot; perception (score between 101 and 150).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The DREEM test showed that the assessment and treatment of pain in dental-maxillary pathology and TMJ dysfunctions through medical rehabilitation by means of balneophysiotherapy is of interest to final year dental medicine students. As a student-teacher partnership, modern education cannot ignore the practical needs of students and should add to their theoretical training with courses and practical training programs necessary in their future profession.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
